sysc-greet for Debian
=====================

Installing the package does not switch greetd over. To use sysc-greet, edit
/etc/greetd/config.toml so the greeter runs inside one of the shipped
compositor configs, as greetd's own _greetd account:

  [default_session]
  user = "_greetd"
  # Hyprland 0.55+:
  command = "start-hyprland -- --config /etc/greetd/hyprland-greeter-config.lua"
  # or sway:
  # command = "sway -c /etc/greetd/sway-greeter-config"
  # or niri:
  # command = "niri -c /etc/greetd/niri-greeter-config.kdl"

then `sudo systemctl restart greetd` (from another VT or over SSH).

Notes
-----

 * The terminal font is JetBrains Mono (fonts-jetbrains-mono) instead of
   upstream's JetBrainsMono Nerd Font; change it in /etc/greetd/kitty.conf.
 * Wallpapers need gSlapper, which Debian does not ship. Without it the
   greeter shows its ASCII backgrounds only.
 * Reboot/shutdown go through logind; /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/
   85-sysc-greet.rules allows them for _greetd.
 * Upstream runs the greeter as its own "greeter" account in
   /var/lib/greeter. This package uses Debian's _greetd instead: the configs
   set HOME=/var/lib/greetd, and its subdirectories come from
   /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/sysc-greet.conf.
